    "created_at": "2019-07-17T14:58:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-07-17T14:58:22Z",
    "body": "This makes rough sense. What could help me understand it better is going through some semi-complex operations and how they move or change things, and thus allow \"collection\". E.g. you seem to have a mental model of how teardown works, but it's not obvious to me exactly which of the above concepts are involved.\r\n\r\nSome operations in particular that would be interesting to see:\r\n\r\n- Same-origin navigation\r\n- Cross-site navigation\r\n- Closing a normal browsing context\r\n- Closing an auxiliary browsing context\r\n- `.remove()`ing an iframe containing a nested browsing context\r\n- Closing or navigating away all documents that are the owner of a given shared/service worker",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
